From 06aef99f5a9fff39a2d5995d125d1f4f275da546 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 07:02:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(compaction): make the summarizer pin resolve, log why,
 and never deadlock
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The pinned compaction summarizer (`agents.<key>.compaction.model`) failed silently.
`resolveCompactionModel` returned the session model on every failure path without
logging anything, and the preemptive-compaction failure log printed the *cached session*
model rather than the resolved target — so a dead pin was indistinguishable from a
working one.

Verified in production over one session: four compaction runs summarized on
`opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` while the config pinned `zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-flash`.
Zero GLM calls were even set up (`llm runtime selected` never named the pinned provider),
each run exceeded the 120s budget, two produced empty summaries, and the context climbed
to 97% before one attempt finally landed. The hook's own log only ever said
"Compaction failed", naming the session model.

Changes:
- `resolveCompactionModelDecision()` returns source/reason/agentName/agentConfigKey/
  pinnedModel so callers can log the decision and tests can assert *why* a model was chosen.
  `resolveCompactionModel()` stays as a thin wrapper (still used by the degradation monitor
  and the anthropic context-window recovery path).
- Observed-agent fallback: the agent is cached alongside the tokens it is cached with, so pin
  resolution no longer depends solely on the in-memory session-agent map.
- Lookup chain: exact key -> case-insensitive -> persona-suffixed base key, with the base
  fallback restricted to canonical agents (`AGENT_DISPLAY_NAMES`) so an unrelated custom
  agent cannot borrow a pinned agent's summarizer.
- Stall release: a summarize that never settles can no longer hold the admission guard
  forever. Attempt tokens ensure a superseded attempt cannot clear a newer attempt's guard,
  and the guard map is hook-owned so `session.deleted` clears it with the rest.
- The degradation monitor's recovery summarize now honours the same pin.
- Tests: pinned key, display name, persona-suffixed variant, custom-agent refusal, missing
  session-agent fallback, no-pin, no-agent, malformed pin, missing config, multi-segment
  model ids, and the stall-release path with its log assertion.

Evidence: tsgo typecheck exit 0; 62 tests across the compaction suites pass; full build
exit 0; bundle markers verified in dist/index.js.
